        ],
        "description": "ART_11 (14e084ed5ca7) claims the idempotency/safety distinction is a category error for append-only log writers\u2014the real invariant is protocol-level distinguishability via delivery metadata. ART_3 (2edd20cc5e66) claims safety is a genuine writer requirement via a layer-boundary distinction (safe writers, idempotent readers). Both share the mechanism of metadata-based distinguishability but contradict on whether calling a writer 'safe' is meaningful or a misnomer.",
        "id": "sha256:2f84c39a8f86498ed1de0ef012d0d19ef48b352e0d35268e777d15439267b915",
        "schema": "bridge.source-conflict.v1"
      },
